IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cca-claims-dates`
IMPORT `cca-claims`

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) -- cases for the claimant's seat (cca-claims.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (C2026C00389), section by section, before the encoding
-- was run. Periods are counted with the day of the event excluded and a year as 12 months (Acts Interpretation Act 1901
-- ss 2G, 36(1), borrowed): "within 3 years after" 10 March 2023 runs to 10 March 2026.
-- HYPOTHETICAL facts throughout. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

GIVEN d IS A DEONTIC `Claim party` `Claim step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ends fulfilled` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

§ `Who is the manufacturer (s 7)`

-- s 7(1)(a): the maker.
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(b), (d): holding out, and letting another hold it out.
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(1)(c), (2)(b): a house brand on the goods it sells is presumed permitted.
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The presumption rebutted: no head holds, and the list is open ("includes").
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(1)(e): an importer when the overseas maker has no Australian place of business.
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The maker has an Australian place of business: the importer is not caught by (e).
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the business a manufacturer of the goods question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Liability for safety defects (ss 138-142, 146)`

-- s 138. Mai is burned by a heater with a safety defect.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the manufacturer is liable to compensate me, and I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against it`
-- No safety defect found.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- Not supplied in trade or commerce (a private sale by the maker).
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- s 146: she was hurt at work and workers' compensation is recoverable.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the loss is one recovered, or recoverable, under a workers' compensation law or a law giving effect to an international agreement (s 146)`
-- s 146 comes before the defences.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the loss is one recovered, or recoverable, under a workers' compensation law or a law giving effect to an international agreement (s 146)`
-- s 142(c): the development-risk defence; s 142(d): a component.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the manufacturer has established a defence (s 142)`
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my injuries question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the manufacturer has established a defence (s 142)`

-- s 139. Mai's partner loses income nursing her.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my loss from another's injury question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the manufacturer is liable to compensate me, and I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against it`
-- s 139(1)(e): her employer's loss comes from a business relationship.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my loss from another's injury question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- No loss of his own.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my loss from another's injury question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my loss from another's injury question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the manufacturer has established a defence (s 142)`

-- s 140. The heater's fire destroys the family's sofa.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged household goods question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the manufacturer is liable to compensate me, and I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against it`
-- A commercial printer is not of a household kind.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged household goods question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- Household-kind goods used in the business.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged household goods question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- s 142(a): the defect arose after supply.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged household goods question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the manufacturer has established a defence (s 142)`

-- s 141. The fire damages the house.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged home or fixtures question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the manufacturer is liable to compensate me, and I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against it`
-- A house let out as an investment: not used privately by the owner.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged home or fixtures question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- A warehouse: not of a kind ordinarily acquired for private use.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged home or fixtures question` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of the section is not met`
-- s 142(b): the defect only because of compliance with a mandatory standard.
#ASSERT `Is the manufacturer liable for my damaged home or fixtures question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the manufacturer has established a defence (s 142)`

-- s 137A: a loss of $100,000, partly caused by the injured person; the court takes off 25%.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover after my share is taken off question` 100000 TRUE 25 EQUALS JUST 75000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover after my share is taken off question` 100000 FALSE 25 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- "(which may be to nil)".
#ASSERT `How much can I recover after my share is taken off question` 100000 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much can I recover after my share is taken off question` 100000 TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 100000
-- A reduction above 100% is not a reduction the section allows.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover after my share is taken off question` 100000 TRUE 120 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Defective goods actions: time, the unknown manufacturer, the court (ss 143-150)`

-- s 143. Aware on 10 March 2023; supplied on 1 June 2015: the 10-year limit (last day 1 June 2025) comes first.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS `on` 1 6 2025
-- Supplied on 1 June 2020: the 3-year limit (10 March 2026) comes first.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS `on` 10 3 2026
-- Aware on 28 February 2024: the period starts on 29 February 2024; 2027 has no 29 February, so it ends with February.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my defective goods action question` (`on` 28 2 2024) (`on` 1 1 2020) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
-- Aware on 29 February 2024: the period starts 1 March 2024 and ends immediately before 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my defective goods action question` (`on` 29 2 2024) (`on` 1 1 2020) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
-- Aware on 31 December 2023: last day 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my defective goods action question` (`on` 31 12 2023) (`on` 1 1 2020) EQUALS `on` 31 12 2026
-- The last day and the day after.
#ASSERT `Am I in time for my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2020) (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I in time for my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2020) (`on` 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The 10-year limit on its last day and the day after.
#ASSERT `Am I in time for my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2015) (`on` 1 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I in time for my defective goods action question` (`on` 10 3 2023) (`on` 1 6 2015) (`on` 2 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 147. The regulative rule: particulars on day 0 and on day 30 are in time; on day 31 they are late.
#ASSERT `s 147 -- particulars on this day are in time` 0 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 147 -- particulars on this day are in time` 30 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 147 -- particulars on this day are in time` 31 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `s 147 -- the supplier must name the manufacturer within 30 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the supplier` `give me particulars identifying the manufacturer, or the supplier's own supplier` 12))) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ends fulfilled` (EVALTRACE `s 147 -- the supplier must name the manufacturer within 30 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 31))) EQUALS FALSE
-- expect: BREACH by the supplier (no particulars within 30 days).
#TRACE `s 147 -- the supplier must name the manufacturer within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- Written request on 1 March 2026. The supplier answers on 31 March (day 30): complied.
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 31 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `no: the supplier gave me the particulars within 30 days`
-- It answers on 1 April (day 31): late; still not knowing at day 30, the supplier is taken to be the manufacturer (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `yes: the supplier is taken to be the manufacturer for my defective goods action (but not for the s 142(c) defence)`
-- No answer, asked on day 30: not yet.
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`on` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `not yet: 30 days have not passed since my request`
-- No answer, day 31.
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `yes: the supplier is taken to be the manufacturer for my defective goods action (but not for the s 142(c) defence)`
-- No answer, but she found the maker herself by day 30.
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `no: I knew who the manufacturer was 30 days after my request`
-- She only telephoned.
#ASSERT `Is the supplier taken to be the manufacturer question` FALSE (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`on` 1 4 2026) EQUALS `no: s 147 works only on a written request to a supplier I know of`

-- s 144.
#ASSERT `Can I recover the whole loss from any one of them question` 2 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I recover the whole loss from any one of them question` 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 148.
#ASSERT `Does the Commonwealth pay me instead question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Commonwealth pay me instead question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Commonwealth pay me instead question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 149(2).
#ASSERT `Can the regulator sue for me question` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the regulator sue for me question` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 150.
#ASSERT `Is the term limiting the manufacturer's liability void question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the term limiting the manufacturer's liability void question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the term limiting the manufacturer's liability void question` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Damages and compensation orders (ss 236, 237; ss 137B, 137C, 137E)`

-- s 236 for misleading conduct causing financial loss.
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against them`
-- s 137C(1): personal injury from misleading conduct.
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: personal injury or death loss cannot be recovered for a Part 2-1 or 3-1 contravention, except from tobacco (s 137C)`
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 3-1 (unfair practices)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: personal injury or death loss cannot be recovered for a Part 2-1 or 3-1 contravention, except from tobacco (s 137C)`
-- The tobacco exception.
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against them`
-- Personal injury from unconscionable conduct: s 137C does not reach Part 2-2 (Part VIB limits it instead).
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 2-2 (unconscionable conduct)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may recover the amount of my loss or damage by action against them`
-- Outside Chapters 2 and 3; no loss; the wrong defendant.
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `another provision` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of s 236(1) is not met`
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 5-4 Division 2 (action for damages against manufacturers for consumer guarantees)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of s 236(1) is not met`
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 3-2 (consumer transactions)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of s 236(1) is not met`
#ASSERT `Can I recover my loss for the contravention question` `Part 3-2 (consumer transactions)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a condition of s 236(1) is not met`

-- s 236(2): 6 years after 15 August 2020 ends 15 August 2026; after 29 February 2020 it ends 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 8 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` FALSE FALSE (`on` 29 2 2020) EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 2 2026)
-- Personal injury from unconscionable conduct: s 236(2) still gives 6 years (Part VIB's limits apply beside it).
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 2-2 (unconscionable conduct)` TRUE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 8 2026)
-- s 137C(2) Note 1: for a tobacco injury from Part 2-1 or 3-1 conduct, Part VIB Division 2 overrides s 236(2).
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE (`on` 15 8 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 3-1 (unfair practices)` TRUE TRUE (`on` 15 8 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Tobacco, but the loss is not personal injury: s 236(2) stands.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my damages action question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` FALSE TRUE (`on` 15 8 2020) EQUALS JUST (`on` 15 8 2026)

-- s 237(3): the last day and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 2-2 (unconscionable conduct)` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 15 8 2026) EQUALS JUST `yes: I may apply in time, and the court may order compensation`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 2-2 (unconscionable conduct)` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 16 8 2026) EQUALS JUST `no: the application is out of time (s 237(3))`
-- s 137E(1): no compensation order for the injury, but the application stands (s 237(2)(b) orders remain).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST `I may apply in time, but the court must not order compensation for the death or personal injury (s 137E(1)): only an order to prevent or reduce the loss`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 3-1 (unfair practices)` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 16 8 2026) EQUALS JUST `no: the application is out of time (s 237(3))`
-- s 137E(2) and its Note: for a tobacco injury Part VIB Division 2 overrides s 237(3), even after 6 years.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST `Part VIB's time limits replace s 237(3) (s 137E(2)): the injury results from tobacco`
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 16 8 2026) EQUALS JUST `Part VIB's time limits replace s 237(3) (s 137E(2)): the injury results from tobacco`
-- No loss suffered or likely.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `Part 3-2 (consumer transactions)` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST `no: a condition of s 237(1) is not met`
-- A provision outside the Parts this encoding lists (a Chapter 4 offence, say).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for a compensation order question` `another provision` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 8 2020) (`on` 1 1 2021) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 137B: $50,000 economic loss from s 18 conduct; the court takes off 40% for the claimant's carelessness.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 EQUALS JUST 30000
-- s 137B(d): no reduction against a fraudster.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST 50000
-- Not economic loss or property damage; not s 18; no carelessness.
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 40 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 40 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `How much can I recover for misleading conduct after my share question` 50000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 150 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Does Part VIB reach my claim (s 87E; ss 137C, 137E)`

#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB applies in full: its time limits and its limits on damages`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 2-2 (unconscionable conduct)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB applies in full: its time limits and its limits on damages`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-3 (safety of consumer goods and product related services)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB applies in full: its time limits and its limits on damages`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-4 (information standards)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB applies in full: its time limits and its limits on damages`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 5-4 Division 2 (action for damages against manufacturers for consumer guarantees)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB applies in full: its time limits and its limits on damages`
-- s 87E(1)(c), (2): tobacco.
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `only Part VIB's time limits (Division 2) and structured settlements (Division 7) apply: the claim is about tobacco`
-- ss 137C, 137E: Part 2-1 and 3-1.
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no personal injury damages can be awarded at all for this contravention (s 137C or s 137E)`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-1 (unfair practices)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no personal injury damages can be awarded at all for this contravention (s 137C or s 137E)`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `only Part VIB's time limits (Division 2) and structured settlements (Division 7) apply: the claim is about tobacco`
-- Parts not listed, and no personal injury damages sought.
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 2-3 (unfair contract terms)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB does not apply to this claim`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-2 (consumer transactions)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB does not apply to this claim`
#ASSERT `Does Part VIB limit my claim question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part VIB does not apply to this claim`

§ `Part VIB time limits (Division 2)`

-- s 87G(1), (4), (5).
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability question` (`on` 1 6 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 1 6 2024
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability question` (`on` 1 6 2024) TRUE (`on` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2024
#ASSERT `What is my date of discoverability question` (`on` 1 6 2024) TRUE (`on` 1 9 2024) EQUALS `on` 1 6 2024

-- s 87G(6). The deceased's date (1 January 2018) fell more than 3 years before death (1 February 2022): it is the earliest.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2018) (`on` 1 2 2022) (`on` 1 6 2022) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 1 2018)
-- Death exactly 3 years on (1 January 2023, the last day of the 3 years): not "more than", so (a) does not apply.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 1 2023) (`on` 1 3 2023) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 3 2023)
-- One day later, (a) applies.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 2 1 2023) (`on` 1 3 2023) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 1 2020)
-- (c): the executor learns after appointment.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 1 2023) (`on` 1 3 2023) FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 9 2023) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 9 2023)
-- Nothing known yet, and (a) does not apply: no date yet.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 1 2023) (`on` 1 3 2023) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a) alone.
#ASSERT `What is the date of discoverability for the deceased's claim question` TRUE (`on` 1 1 2018) (`on` 1 2 2022) (`on` 1 6 2022) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (`on` 1 1 2018)

-- s 87F, 87H. Discovered 1 June 2024, act 1 January 2024: 3 years ends 1 June 2027; long stop 1 January 2036.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 1 6 2027
-- Discovered late (1 March 2033) for an act on 1 January 2022: the long stop (1 January 2034) comes first.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2034
-- s 87H(2): an extension to 1 January 2037 is capped at 3 years beyond discoverability (1 March 2036).
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 TRUE (`on` 1 1 2037) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2036
-- An extension to 1 June 2035, within the cap.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 TRUE (`on` 1 6 2035) EQUALS `on` 1 6 2035
-- s 87F(1A): no long stop for tobacco.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2036
-- s 87J: 100 days without a capable guardian: 1 June 2027 plus 100 days is 9 September 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 100 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 9 9 2027
-- s 87K: abused at 7 by a guardian (act 1 January 2010, discovered 1 January 2012), turning 25 on 15 May 2027:
-- counting starts on 15 May 2027, so 3 years ends 14 May 2030 (the long stop, 14 May 2039, is later).
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 1 2012) (`on` 1 1 2010) FALSE TRUE (`on` 15 5 2027) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 14 5 2030
-- The same facts without s 87K: the 3 years ended 1 January 2015.
#ASSERT `By when must I start my personal injury claim question` (`on` 1 1 2012) (`on` 1 1 2010) FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 5 2027) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `on` 1 1 2015

-- Out of time? On the last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` FALSE (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` FALSE (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 2 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Late discovery: started 2 January 2034, the day after the long stop.
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 3-5 (liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)` FALSE (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 2 1 2034) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A tobacco claim for misleading conduct: Division 2 applies (s 137C(2)) without the long stop: in time.
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2033) (`on` 1 1 2022) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 2 1 2034) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Division 2 does not reach the claim.
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 2-3 (unfair contract terms)` FALSE (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 2 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my personal injury claim out of time question` `Part 2-1 (misleading or deceptive conduct)` FALSE (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) 0 FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 2 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part VIB limits on damages for non-economic loss (Division 3)`

-- s 87M.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum for non-economic loss for the year question` 2004 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 250000
-- 250,000 x 150/148 = 253,378.38..., to the nearest $10: 253,380.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum for non-economic loss for the year question` 2005 250000 150 148 EQUALS JUST 253380
